# QA M6 regression (was qa_m6_bug_sabre_over_bench; fixed by D-102, E42):
# file C's sabre must not hurt Resi standing still on the bench (cols
# 249-250), the 2-high pen wall the file turns at and the stage's designed
# perch between singer #2 and the file (game-design Stage 8 section 5).
# The solver's route to the theatre street (bad_ischl_file_c_singer's
# first 1340 frames), 136 idle frames (a later arrival, so the file wakes
# later and turns at the bench in another drill phase), then onto the
# bench: from about 1880 she stands on it, hitbox x 4011-4023 (the bench
# ends at 4016), feet on its top (208). File C marches left to the bench,
# the front officer halts 3 px from it (x 4019, Habt Acht 2089) and
# presents at 2113 (drill f 192). The bug: his 8x16 sabre zone (x
# 4021-4029, y 202-218) reached 6 px above the bench top into her feet and
# she died (Normal) without moving. Since D-102 the zone is 8x10 (the drawn
# blade), it ends 32 px above his feet, level with the bench top (strict
# overlap), and she stays.
# Re-cut for D-102 (E42): B2's stone end pier (237, rows 7-10, with the
# bridge at (236, row 8)) blocks the old stop on the 1-high flower box, so
# from 1613 she runs, hops onto the box top, jumps the pier and stops on
# the street (1661), runs and jumps from there over singer #2 onto the
# bench (1730-1835) and brakes to the old resting x (1836-1910); from 1911
# on her positions are the old ones (the file woke before 1613, so the
# drill is unchanged: the front officer presents at x 4019 at 2113).
# Expected: a player standing on a pen wall is never hurt by an officer in
# the pen below (deaths=0, still on the bench at the end).
level  = bad_ischl
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 no_event=Hurt no_event=Died state=playing player_y<=186 player_x>=4011
